note split.om: the error 12 fix. Same value, two helpers, each with few live names
note blend = s1 + s2 + (s3 + df) + (ab + cd + ef) = 2 * (ab + cd + ef) + (ac + bd + ce + df)
fn prods a ulong b ulong c ulong d ulong e ulong f ulong to ulong
ret add add mul a b mul c d mul e f
end
fn mixes a ulong b ulong c ulong d ulong e ulong f ulong to ulong
ret add add add a c add b d add xor c e xor d f
end
fn blend a ulong b ulong c ulong d ulong e ulong f ulong to ulong
p = prods a b c d e f
m = mixes a b c d e f
ret add add p p m
end
fn putnum v ulong to long
note write v in decimal and a newline. A ulong has at most 20 digits, so bound 20 is proved
d = new uchar 21 0
o = new uchar 21 0
n = ulong 0
x = v
while true bound 20
put d n uchar add rem x 10 48
n = add n 1
x = div x 10
if eq x 0
break
end
end
for i ulong n
put o i get d sub sub n i 1
end
put o n 10
w = write 1 o 0 add n 1
ret w
end
fn blendref a ulong b ulong c ulong d ulong e ulong f ulong to ulong
note the refused body, one sum at a time, so fewer names are live at once: the reference
ab = mul a b
cd = mul c d
ef = mul e f
t = add add ab cd add ef add a c
t = add t add add b d xor c e
t = add t xor d f
t = add t add add ab cd ef
ret t
end
fn main to int
x = blend 1 2 3 4 5 6
if ne x blendref 1 2 3 4 5 6
ret 3
end
w = putnum x
x = blend 7 0 9 2 11 3
if ne x blendref 7 0 9 2 11 3
ret 4
end
w = putnum x
ret 0
end
